  <h2 id="civil-services">Where civil services actually fits</h2>

  <p>
    Civil services deserves its own honest placement on this list, because it is often treated as the default "best" humanities career by families, without a clear look at the actual odds and pay.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--gold">
    <p>
      An entry-level IAS officer's basic pay starts at Rs 56,100 a month under the 7th Pay Commission, roughly Rs 98,000-1,03,000 in-hand in a metro city once allowances are included, rising toward Rs 2,50,000 basic at the most senior level over a full career.
    </p>
    <p>
      The selection ratio across roughly 10 lakh applicants for about 1,000-1,100 posts each cycle is close to 0.1%. That does not make the exam not worth attempting, but it does mean most humanities students preparing for it should also seriously map at least one path from this ranking as a parallel option, not an afterthought.
    </p>
  </div>

